alculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle saw April to May at 185% of normal and November to December at 34%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 40% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 19042 at 52%.</p>"}
